{"name":"Kitchen Terra Cotta","hex":"#c0816e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kitchen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A room or area for preparing food.","Cuisine; style of cooking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To do kitchen work; to prepare food.","To embellish a basic food; to season, add condiments, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitchen"},{"term":"terra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A geologic and geographic region of a celestial body which is a highland analogous to a continent or large landmass."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Earth, soil, land, or ground as a physical surface.","The material world as opposed to the heavens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terra"},{"term":"cotta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A surplice, in England and America usually one shorter and less full than the ordinary surplice and with short sleeves, or sometimes none.","A kind of coarse woolen blanket."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of katha (“unit of area”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Terracotta","blocks":[{"text":"Terracotta, also known as terra cotta or terra-cotta, is a clay-based non-vitreous ceramic fired at relatively low temperatures. The term is used for earthenware objects of certain types, as set out below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Bust_of_the_Virgin_MET_DP124049_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bust_of_the_Virgin_MET_DP124049_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terracotta","wikidata":"Q60424"},{"title":"Kitchen","blocks":[{"text":"A kitchen is a room or part of a room used for cooking and food preparation in a dwelling or in a commercial establishment. A modern middle-class residential kitchen is typically equipped with a stove, a sink with hot and cold running water, a refrigerator, and worktops and kitchen cabinets arranged according to a modular design. Many households have a microwave oven, a dishwasher, and other electric appliances. The main functions of a kitchen are to store, prepare and cook food. The room or area may also be used for dining, entertaining and laundry. The design and construction of kitchens is a huge market all over the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/La_cuisine_%28mus%C3%A9e_dart_nouveau%2C_Riga%29_%287563655820%29.jpg/330px-La_cuisine_%28mus%C3%A9e_dart_nouveau%2C_Riga%29_%287563655820%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitchen","wikidata":"Q43164"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Pentola_in_terracotta.jpg/500px-Pentola_in_terracotta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Pentola_in_terracotta.jpg/1280px-Pentola_in_terracotta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Pentola_in_terracotta.jpg/500px-Pentola_in_terracotta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glazed terracotta casserole dish","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APentola_in_terracotta.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Female_terracotta_figurines_-_Mohenjo-daro_-_BM.jpg/500px-Female_terracotta_figurines_-_Mohenjo-daro_-_BM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Female_terracotta_figurines_-_Mohenjo-daro_-_BM.jpg/1280px-Female_terracotta_figurines_-_Mohenjo-daro_-_BM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip